// Title: Potential File Download Via MS-AppInstaller Protocol Handler
// Sigma ID: 180c7c5c-d64b-4a63-86e9-68910451bc8b
// Status: test | Level: medium
// Author: Nasreddine Bencherchali (Nextron Systems), Swachchhanda Shrawan Poudel
// Date: 2023-11-09 | Modified: -
// ATT&CK: execution, stealth, T1218
// Description: Detects usage of the "ms-appinstaller" protocol handler via command line to potentially download
//   arbitrary files via AppInstaller.EXE The downloaded files are temporarily stored in ":\Users\%us
//   ername%\AppData\Local\Packages\Microsoft.DesktopAppInstaller_8wekyb3d8bbwe\AC\INetCache\<RANDOM-
//   8-CHAR-DIRECTORY>"
// False positives:
//   - Unknown
// References:
//   - https://lolbas-project.github.io/lolbas/Binaries/AppInstaller/
// Sigma rule: https://github.com/SigmaHQ/sigma/blob/92723d79577e893b7e3090ed7ea1861f865bfd5e/rules/windows/process_creation/proc_creation_win_susp_ms_appinstaller_download.yml
// License: Detection Rule License (DRL) 1.1 - https://github.com/SigmaHQ/Detection-Rule-License
// Converted by sigma2kql (target: microsoft_xdr, pySigma 1.5.1, pySigma-backend-kusto 1.0.1)
// Validation: passed (Kusto.Language, Defender schema)
// Machine-generated and not tested against real telemetry. Verify before use as a detection.

DeviceProcessEvents
| where (ProcessCommandLine contains "ms-appinstaller://" and ProcessCommandLine contains "source=") and ProcessCommandLine contains "http"
